      "§rThe walls are closing, they’re crushing, squishing, flattening, sealing around §1me§r, the hallway forming around §1my§r body to fit §1me§r like an impossible suit, twisting and contorting me, but it doesn’t. \n\n\nNothing is happening. ",
      "§1I§r can’t bear to look up. §1I§r know if §1I§r look at that wall again it’ll be much closer.\n\n§0If §1I§r just don’t look, §1I§r can pretend §1I’m§r not in a compressing nightmare. Just imagine the §2Library§r as §1I’ve§r experienced it so far.\n\nThose long, winding stairs, the huge",
